[Event "Dutch: Leningrad"]

{The Dutch (1...f5) grabs e4 and aims for a kingside attack. The Leningrad combines it with a g7 fianchetto.}
1. d4 {Centre. The pawn on d4 controls e5.}
1... f5 {[%csl Ge4] The Dutch. The pawn on f5 controls e4.}
2. g3 {Fianchetto.}
2... Nf6 {Develops. The knight on f6 controls d5 and e4.}
3. Bg2 {Long diagonal. The bishop on g2 eyes the pawn on b7 and controls d5 and e4.}
3... g6 {Fianchetto.}
4. Nf3 {Develops. The knight on f3 controls e5.}
4... Bg7 {Develops.}
5. O-O {Castles. The king is safe and the rook comes into play.}
5... O-O {Castles. The king is safe and the rook comes into play.}
6. c4 {Space. The pawn on c4 controls d5.}
6... d6 {Prepares ...e5. The pawn on d6 controls e5.}
7. Nc3 {Develops. The knight on c3 controls d5 and e4.}
7... Qe8 {Prepares ...e5 and ...Qh5.}
 (7... c6 {Flexible: prepares ...Qa5 or ...Na6. The pawn on c6 controls d5.}
8. d5 {Gains space. The pawn on d5 eyes the pawn on c6.}
)
8. d5 {Gains space.}
8... a5 {Stops b4.} *

[Event "Dutch: Anti-Dutch lines"]

{2.Bg5, 2.Nc3, 2.e4 and the London.}
1. d4 {Centre. The pawn on d4 controls e5.}
1... f5 {Dutch. The pawn on f5 controls e4.}
2. Bf4 {The London. The bishop on f4 eyes the pawn on c7 and controls e5.}
 (2. e4 {The Staunton Gambit. The pawn on e4 eyes the pawn on f5 and controls d5.}
2... fxe4 {Takes.}
3. Nc3 {Develops. The knight on c3 eyes the pawn on e4 and controls d5.}
3... Nf6 {Develops. The knight on f6 controls d5.}
4. Bg5 {Pins. The bishop on g5 eyes the knight on f6.}
4... g6 {Fianchetto.}
5. f3 {Opens lines. The pawn on f3 eyes the pawn on e4.}
5... exf3 {Takes. The pawn on f3 eyes the pawn on g2.}
6. Nxf3 {Recaptures. The knight on f3 controls e5.}
6... Bg7 {Develops.}
)
 (2. Nc3 {Develops. The knight on c3 controls d5 and e4.}
2... Nf6 {Develops. The knight on f6 controls d5 and e4.}
3. Bg5 {Pins. The bishop on g5 eyes the knight on f6.}
3... d5 {Centre. The pawn on d5 controls e4.}
4. Bxf6 {Trades. The bishop on f6 eyes the pawn on e7 and the pawn on g7 and controls e5.}
4... exf6 {Recaptures. The pawn on f6 controls e5.}
5. e3 {Solid.}
5... c6 {Solid.}
)
2... Nf6 {Develops. The knight on f6 controls d5 and e4.}
3. e3 {Solid.}
3... g6 {Fianchetto.}
4. Nf3 {Develops. The knight on f3 controls e5.}
4... Bg7 {Develops.}
5. h3 {Prepares Be2.}
5... O-O {Castles. The king is safe and the rook comes into play.} *
